"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Introduction\n","**Purpose and Scenario:**\n","This case study is conducted for **Cyclistic**, a fictional bike-share company based in Chicago featuring over 5,800 bicycles and 600 docking stations. As a junior data analyst working on the marketing analyst team under Director Lily Moreno, the core business objective is driven by a critical realization: the company's future economic growth and success depend heavily on maximizing the number of annual memberships, as annual members are significantly more profitable than casual riders. \n","\n","**The Real-World Obstacle & Strategy:**\n","Rather than launching a broad marketing campaign to target entirely new customers, the marketing team identified a prime opportunity to convert existing casual riders—who are already familiar with the program and use the bikes for their mobility needs—into dedicated annual members. However, before executive leadership can approve any strategic marketing programs, the recommendations must be rigorously backed by compelling data insights and professional visualizations. \n","\n","**Analytical Framework:**\n","To tackle this business challenge, this project strictly follows the industry-standard six-step data analysis process outlined in the Google Data Analytics framework: **Ask, Prepare, Process, Analyze, Share, and Act**."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"bc89ea66","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002737,"end_time":"2026-09-13T14:00:15.003554+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-13T14:00:15.000817+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 2. Problems\n","**Major Problem Identification:**\n","The primary problem under investigation is defined by the first guiding question assigned by management: **\"How do annual members and casual riders use Cyclistic bikes differently?\"** Without isolating these behavioral patterns, the team cannot design targeted digital media strategies.\n","\n","**Analysis Approach & Data Scope:**\n","To uncover these behavioral gaps, I am utilizing *Python (Pandas)* to process and analyze historical trip data covering the past 12 consecutive months, spanning from September 2025 through August 2026.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"f9785695","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-13T14:00:15.010852Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-13T14:00:15.010299Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-13T14:00:45.925808Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-13T14:00:45.924917Z"},"papermill":{"duration":30.923649,"end_time":"2026-09-13T14:00:45.92986+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-13T14:00:15.006211+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Total rows and columns: (6115982, 13)\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>ride_id</th>\n","      <th>rideable_type</th>\n","      <th>started_at</th>\n","      <th>ended_at</th>\n","      <th>start_station_name</th>\n","      <th>start_station_id</th>\n","      <th>end_station_name</th>\n","      <th>end_station_id</th>\n","      <th>start_lat</th>\n","      <th>start_lng</th>\n","      <th>end_lat</th>\n","      <th>end_lng</th>\n","      <th>member_casual</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0</th>\n","      <td>FD0EB1D32AF0D47E</td>\n","      <td>classic_bike</td>\n","      <td>2026-01-31 09:13:09.018</td>\n","      <td>2026-01-31 09:28:10.302</td>\n","      <td>Central St &amp; Girard Ave</td>\n","      <td>CHI02042</td>\n","      <td>Dodge Ave &amp; Church St</td>\n","      <td>CHI00741</td>\n","      <td>42.