.head()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a6569c72","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.003139,"end_time":"2026-09-13T14:01:11.285204+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-13T14:01:11.282065+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3. Solutions\n","\n","*Proposed Solution:* \n","\n","To convert casual riders into annual members, Cyclistic should launch targeted digital media campaigns focused on the behavioral differences uncovered in our 12-month analysis. Specifically, since casual riders take significantly longer trips (averaging ~20.7 minutes compared to ~12.4 minutes for members) and peak heavily during weekends, marketing initiatives should introduce weekend-focused promotional bundles, leisure-to-commuter loyalty incentives, and digital app notifications highlighting cost savings for longer recreational rides.\n","\n","*Alternatives:* \n","\n","We also evaluated broad-spectrum billboard and transit station advertisements targeting general tourists; however, this approach lacks personalized engagement and yields lower conversion efficiency compared to digital media.\n","\n","*Pros and Cons:* \n","\n","Digital app-based promotions offer high precision, direct tracking, and cost-effectiveness, though they require active user engagement on the mobile app. Broad advertisements build general brand awareness but fail to capture direct conversion metrics."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"15e5be8e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-13T14:01:11.293397Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-13T14:01:11.292956Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-13T14:01:13.014419Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-13T14:01:13.013261Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.727978,"end_time":"2026-09-13T14:01:13.016352+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-13T14:01:11.288374+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["--- Overall Ride Length Summary (Minutes) ---\n","count    6.115918e+06\n